.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt ZKCMP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zkcmp
.Nd zero-knowledge file comparison utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm -c
.Op Fl h Ar hash
.Ar file
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm -p
.Op Fl h Ar hash
.Ar file
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl h Ar hash
.Ar commit
.Ar proof
.Pp
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility provides zero-knowledge comparison and proof operations for files.
It allows a prover to demonstrate that a file matches a commitment without
revealing the file's cryptographic hash.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm zkcmp -c Ar file
Generate a Base64-encoded public commitment for
.Ar file.
.It Cm zkcmp -p Ar file
Generate a Base64-encoded zero-knowledge proof for
.Ar file .
.It Cm zkcmp Ar commit Ar proof
Verify a zero-knowledge proof against a public commitment.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h Ar hash
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar sha256
SHA-256 is the default.
.It Ar sha3-256
.It Ar sha512-256
.El
.El
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s
Silent mode; return exit status only.
.El
.Sh PROTOCOL
The zero-knowledge protocol is based on a Schnorr-style proof using the
3072-bit Modular Exponentiation Group defined by RFC 3526.

The file is hashed using the selected hash algorithm.
The resulting digest is used to derive the secret value for the proof.
The proof uses a Fiat-Shamir challenge to provide a non-interactive
verification protocol.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a commitment for a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zkcmp -c file > commit
.Ed

Generate a proof for a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zkcmp -p file > proof
.Ed

Verify a commitment and proof:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zkcmp commit proof
.Ed

Generate a commitment and proof once and allow multiple parties to verify
them independently:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zkcmp -c file > commit
$ zkcmp -p file > proof
$ zkcmp commit proof
$ ssh host1 'zkcmp commit proof'
$ ssh host2 'zkcmp commit proof'
.Ed

Use SHA3-256 for proof generation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zkcmp -p -h sha3-256 file
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The operation completed or the proof verified successfully.
.It 1
The proof did not match.
.It 2
An operational error occurred.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmp 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Sh AUTHOR
.An Nami Arjmandi
.El
